<title>UK: Cater Allen surges on bid hopes.</title>
<headline>Cater Allen surges on bid hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cater Allen Holdings Plc surged some 25 percent on Thursday after the UK financial services group said it was in talks that could lead to an offer.</p>
<p>At 1057 GMT, the shares were up 108-1/2 to 550, just 2-1/2p off a three-and-a-half year high set earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;There had been rumours for months that Cater Allen could be a takeover target,&quot; said one market maker. &quot;It's anyone's guess what the (bid) price will be if there's an offer.&quot;</p>
<p>The company said an announcement would be made &quot;in due course&quot; but gave no details. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
